    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, including the new GOLD test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`) passes and the build succeeds.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe GOLD rule needs to be evaluated **at create time** (\"has 3+ members *after this create*\") and be readable later via `GET`, so I mirrored the existing `namesakeCount` \u2192 SILVER pattern: count at create, persist the count, let the mapper read it. Each unit I touched stays small and low-complexity.\n\n- **`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`** (new) \u2014 a one-method pipeline step (WMC_other = 0) that counts owners sharing the already-assigned `householdId`, seeded at 1 for the not-yet-saved owner.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `countHousehold` step after `countNamesakes` (the `householdId` is assigned earlier by `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`), before `save`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdSize` field with a plain getter/setter, alongside `namesakeCount`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` gains one leading `if`: GOLD when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic is untouched.\n- **Schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `household_size` column so all four stay consistent with `household_id`/`namesake_count`.\n- **Data** (`hsqldb`, `mysql`) \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts; `h2`/`postgres` use explicit column lists and needed no change.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the now-stale `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nNotes on structural impact: I kept the create-time semantics (each owner's tier is frozen at its own create \u2014 the third member is GOLD, earlier members keep their create-time tier) rather than recomputing on read, which is the correct reading of the spec. The mapper edit is a single added branch, the new counting logic lives in its own zero-context class, and the entity change is just field+accessors.",
